Subject: [PATCH] Service actual native hardware at the original RFL wait
Upstream-base: 2c5c51e483b652d178ef06a44b83b07a0f97d2a6

Only the native SDK wait invokes the existing owner hardware/yield boundary.
Original status, callbacks, console code and source requests are unchanged.
Full RFL resource initialization remains a separate qualification.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_System.c b/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_System.c
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_System.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/rfl/RFL_System.c
@@ -224,6 +224,13 @@
 
     do {
         status = RFLGetAsyncStatus();
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+        // The native owner delivers actual hardware interrupts at SDK waits.
+        // This preserves the source status predicate and completion callbacks.
+        if (status == RFLErrcode_Busy) {
+            OSYieldThread();
+        }
+#endif
     } while (status == RFLErrcode_Busy);
 
     return status;
